Additional grant for Rampart mobile store binaries
Copyright 2026 Jesse Mosier-Bowers, operating as Operation Locked In

Jesse Mosier-Bowers, as copyright holder of Rampart, additionally licenses
the iOS and Android store binaries of Rampart under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (the file licenses/APACHE-2.0.txt in this repository).

You may use, copy, modify, and distribute those mobile binaries under
Apache License 2.0. You may also use the same source under the GNU
General Public License version 3 (the file LICENSE). You choose which
grant to take.

Desktop builds (Windows, macOS, Linux) remain GNU GPLv3 only.

This additional grant exists because Apple’s App Store terms add
restrictions that GPLv3 does not allow a licensee to impose. Apache-2.0
does not forbid those extra terms, so a store binary can be submitted
in good faith. The source stays public either way.

DnsClient.NET remains Apache License 2.0 in every build.
